# The application's own domain: the Android app's own page, and the chat's
# functionality the app talks to (api/ and media.php, one-line loaders of the
# chat's own files). What people SEE here is the application's page - the
# website chat's pages are not served from this domain (owner, 19 Sep 2026:
# "application ki UI/UX same rahegi, sirf functionality chat jaisi").
DirectoryIndex index.html

# The download page's address given out earlier the same day.
RedirectMatch 302 ^/app/?$ /

# The APK is handed to GitHub's download network, and the address people already
# have keeps working. THIS host closes a transfer that lasts longer than about
# four minutes: measured on 22 September 2026, a phone at 150 KB/s was cut off at
# 38.6 of 63.5 MB, and three of five downloads at once were cut at 5.5, 18.3 and
# 30.9 MB. A cut download leaves a half-written file, and Android reports that as
# "there was a problem parsing the package" - which is exactly what customers saw.
# The release is public and holds the APK alone; no code is published with it.
RedirectMatch 302 ^/SBK-Chat\.apk$ https://github.com/MohsinRaza2000/SBK-APK/releases/download/v1.0.9/SBK-Chat.apk
